# Agent / tooling working dirs (not part of the project)
#
# .beads/ data never enters git. This repository is PUBLIC and the backlog
# holds real wallet addresses, so bead text lives only in the Dolt tracker,
# whose remote is a private repository, never this one. Only the tracker's
# scaffolding (config.yaml, README.md, hooks/, metadata.json, .gitignore) is
# committed. These lines repeat the data rules of .beads/.gitignore so the
# protection does not depend on that file alone.
.beads/*.jsonl
.beads/embeddeddolt/
.beads/dolt/
.beads/backup/
.beads/*.db
.beads/.beads-credential-key
.beads/.local_version
.omc/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.sddw/
.superset/
.tbd/

# Agent working files. These are scratch, not documentation, and they must never
# be committed: they carried this project's internal planning verbatim, quoted
# the maintainer directly, and printed a real node identity address — all of
# which was then published to the public docs site, because MkDocs builds every
# file in docs_dir whether or not it appears in nav.
docs/GOAL.md
docs/AUTOPILOT-WORKLOG.md
docs/DEFERRED-QUESTIONS.md
